Z||000003||BN Boomer||01-03-2001||05:47 PM||||Does it <I>slant</I> to the right or <B>pull</B> to the right when you are driving it? If it actually <I>slants</I>, you probably have big suspension problems. If it just <B>pulls</B>, you probably just need an alignment.||||reg||1
Z||000004||jerpro||01-03-2001||05:55 PM||||sorry it's a pull not a slant.<BR>but thanks. I hope there is nothing else wrong with it.<BR>I have also noticed that when I slightly turn the steering wheel to the left I hear a light intermitent squeaking from the front left wheel.<BR>WHat could this be?<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Indiana_resto_guy||01-03-2001||07:45 PM||||If the car is pre '88, you may want to check the wheel bearings ASAP. Sounds possible that a cage may have broken (some stock ones had plastic cages). Also check the caliper mounting, may be jambed up and no longer square (dragging pads-replace them). Nothing of any big deal if checked in a hurry. Get a new alignment after service if pull remains!||||reg||1
